---
/**
 * /terms — terms of use.
 *
 * ⚠️ Technically accurate draft, NOT legal advice. Have it reviewed by a
 * Nigerian lawyer before relying on it.
 *
 * The disclaimer sections below matter commercially, not just legally: this site
 * gives electrical installation guidance and publishes price estimates, and both
 * carry real risk if a reader treats them as guarantees.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, BUSINESS } from '../config/site';

const pageUrl = `${SITE.url}/terms/`;
const lastUpdated = '5 October 2026';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  '@id': `${pageUrl}#webpage`,
  url: pageUrl,
  name: 'Terms of Use',
  dateModified: '2026-10-05',
  inLanguage: 'en-NG',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms governing use of IbadanSolarHub.com.ng, including the limits of our solar sizing estimates, price data and installer referrals."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="bg-slate-900 text-white py-12 border-b border-slate-800">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black tracking-tight">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 space-y-8 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">1. Acceptance</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        By using {SITE.name} you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use
        the site. The site is operated by {BUSINESS.legalName}.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/*
      This is the single most important section on the page. Please do not soften
      it without legal advice — the sizing output is guidance, not a specification.
    */}
    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-amber-900">2. Sizing Estimates Are Guidance, Not Guarantees</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-amber-900">
        <p>
          <strong>Our calculator produces an estimate.</strong> It is built from the appliance
          ratings and run hours you enter, using the methodology published on our
          <a href="/about" class="font-semibold underline underline-offset-2">About page</a>.
          Its accuracy depends entirely on the accuracy of what you enter.
        </p>
        <p>
          It does not know your actual appliance power ratings, your roof orientation, shading,
          cable lengths, ambient temperatures, battery health, or the real-world efficiency of
          the specific equipment you buy. It is not a substitute for a physical site survey by a
          qualified installer.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Always obtain a site inspection before purchasing or installing a system.</strong>
          We are not liable for a system that underperforms, trips, or fails to meet your needs
          where our estimate was used without professional verification.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">3. Price Information</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Equipment prices and turnkey installation ranges published on this site are estimates
        gathered from retailers, distributors and installer quotes. The Naira is volatile,
        import duties change, and stock availability varies. Prices are indicative benchmarks
        only. Always confirm the current price directly with the vendor or installer before
        committing to any purchase.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">4. Estimator and Installer Referrals</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We refer enquiries to third-party solar installers. Those installers are independent
        businesses. We are not their employer, agent or partner, and we do not supervise,
        warrant or guarantee their work, pricing, timelines or warranties.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Any contract for installation is between you and the installer. We may receive a
        referral fee from installers, which does not increase the price you pay. You are
        responsible for verifying any installer's credentials, certifications and warranty
        terms before hiring them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">5. Affiliate Links</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        This site contains affiliate links to retailers and financing partners. We may earn a
        commission if you click through and make a purchase or sign up, at no additional cost
        to you. See our
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure" class="font-semibold text-solar-700 underline underline-offset-2">affiliate disclosure</a>
        for the full list and our editorial independence commitment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">6. Electrical Safety</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Solar and inverter installations involving mains voltage, battery banks and DC arrays
        are hazardous and must be carried out by competent, qualified persons. Nothing on this
        site is instructions for self-installation. Do not attempt to install, modify or repair
        an electrical system yourself based on information published here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">7. Digital Products</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Our digital downloads (spreadsheets, guides and toolkits) are sold through Selar and are
        subject to Selar's checkout, delivery and refund terms. Because they are digital goods
        delivered instantly, they are generally non-refundable once downloaded. They are for your
        own use and may not be redistributed or resold.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">8. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The written content, research reports, calculator, data compilations and design of this
        site are owned by {BUSINESS.legalName} unless otherwise stated. You may quote short
        extracts with a link back to the source page. You may not republish our research or
        data compilations in full, or use them to train or populate a competing commercial
        product, without written permission.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The site and all content are provided "as is". To the fullest extent permitted by
        Nigerian law, we exclude liability for any indirect, incidental or consequential loss
        arising from your use of this site, including loss arising from reliance on sizing
        estimates, price information, or the work of any third-party installer we refer you to.
        Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">10. Availability</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We aim to keep the site available but do not guarantee uninterrupted access. We may
        change, suspend or withdraw any part of the site, including the calculator and research
        content, without notice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">11. Governing Law</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, and disputes
        are subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Nigerian courts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">12. Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Questions about these terms:
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="font-semibold text-solar-700 underline underline-offset-2">{SITE.email}</a>
        or via our <a href="/contact" class="font-semibold text-solar-700 underline underline-offset-2">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6">
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-slate-700">Note for the site owner:</strong> this is a good-faith,
        technically accurate draft reflecting how the site actually operates. It is not legal
        advice. Have a Nigerian lawyer review sections 2, 4 and 9 in particular — those carry
        the most commercial risk.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
